  },
  {
    id: "synergee-games-barbell",
    name: "Synergee Games Barbell",
    category: "Multi-purpose bar with needle bearings, 15 or 20 kg",
    badge: "Best Value",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Synergee+Games+20kg+Barbell&tag=sktiger-20",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "$150–$240",
    priceBounds: {"low":150,"high":240},
    specs: "15 or 20 kg · 28 mm shaft (20 kg), 25 mm (15 kg) · 190,000 PSI and 1,500 lb (maker) · needle bearings · 1.2 mm diamond knurl, dual marks, no center knurl",
    pros: [
      "The same 190,000 PSI and 1,500 lb figures as bars costing far more, per Synergee and BarBend",
      "Needle bearings spin fast, which suits cleans, snatches and conditioning work",
      "Sold in 15 and 20 kg versions, both on Synergee's store and on Amazon",
      "Medium knurl that reviewers describe as comfortable for high-rep sessions",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Garage Gym Reviews says the fast spin can feel unstable under heavy, slow lifts",
      "Both review sites say the coated sleeves scuff and scratch easily",
      "No center knurl",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The best bar for the money, and the strongest-rated bar we found on Amazon. Choose a bushing bar instead if you mostly squat and deadlift heavy.",
    description: "Synergee is best known as an Amazon brand, and its Games bar is the multi-purpose bar both review sites recommend for buyers who want good specifications for less. Synergee lists the 20 kg bar with a 28 mm shaft, 16.4-inch loadable sleeves, ten sets of needle bearings, a 1.2 mm diamond knurl with dual marks, a 190,000 PSI tensile strength and a 1,500 lb capacity; BarBend gives the same strength, rating, diameter and bearings. The 15 kg version has a 25 mm shaft and 13-inch sleeves. Synergee's store showed $149.95 for the 15 kg bar and $169.95 for the 20 kg bar on 19 October 2026, while the review sites quoted $179.95 and $239.95 earlier in the year, so prices clearly move. Two details did not line up: Synergee lists the 20 kg bar at 86.36 inches and the Amazon listing at 86.75 inches, and Synergee now calls the finish a ceramic coating where older listings say Cerakote. Reviews list a lifetime warranty; Synergee's own description did not state the term when we checked, so it is not on the card. The bearings are the main thing to weigh: they spin fast and freely, which weightlifters like, and Garage Gym Reviews notes they can feel less controlled under very heavy loads.",
  },
  {
    id: "rogue-ohio-bar",
    name: "Rogue Ohio Bar",
    category: "Multi-purpose 20 kg bar, made in the USA",
    badge: "Made in USA",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/s?k=olympic+barbell&tag=sktiger-20",
    amazonLabel: "Shop Similar on Amazon",
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "$305–$365",
    priceBounds: {"low":305,"high":365},
    specs: "20 kg · 28.5 mm shaft · 190,000 PSI (maker) · bronze bushings · dual marks, no center knurl · 16.4 in. loadable sleeves · lifetime warranty against defects and bending",
    pros: [
      "Made in the USA, and one of the most widely used multi-purpose bars in the world",
      "More finish choices than any other bar here, including Cerakote and stainless steel",
      "Rogue's warranty covers bending as well as defects",
      "Bronze bushings give a consistent spin with little maintenance",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Sold only through Rogue's own store, not on Amazon",
      "Costs more than the REP Colorado for the same headline figures",
      "Garage Gym Reviews notes the bushings spin more slowly than an Olympic lifter may want",
    ],
    bottomLine: "Buy it if made-in-USA steel or a stainless or Cerakote finish matters to you. Otherwise the Colorado does the same job for less.",
    description: "The Ohio Bar is the bar many home gyms are built around, and Garage Gym Reviews names it its best Olympic barbell for home gyms. Rogue lists the black zinc version at 20 kg and 86.75 inches overall, with a 28.5 mm shaft, 16.40-inch loadable sleeves, precision-machined bronze bushings, a medium multi-purpose knurl with dual marks, no center knurl and a tensile strength of 190,000 PSI. Garage Gym Reviews gives the same strength, diameter and bushings and calls the knurl fairly passive. Rogue's lifetime warranty covers construction defects and bending, which is more than most. On 19 October 2026 Rogue charged $305 for the black zinc bar and $365 for the Cerakote version; it also sells stainless steel, E-coat and black oxide versions, and Garage Gym Reviews suggests the stainless or Cerakote finishes if your gym is damp. The case against it is price, not quality: the REP Colorado has the same tensile strength, a similar shaft and a lifetime warranty for less. Rogue does not sell through Amazon, so the button runs an Amazon search for comparable bars rather than this one; buy the Ohio Bar from Rogue's store.",
  },
  {
    id: "fringe-sport-wonder-bar",
    name: "Fringe Sport Wonder Bar V2 (20 kg)",
    category: "Multi-purpose bar with bushings or bearings",
    badge: "Bushing or Bearing",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/s?k=olympic+barbell&tag=sktiger-20",
    amazonLabel: "Shop Similar on Amazon",
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "$299–$319",
    priceBounds: {"low":299,"high":319},
    specs: "20 kg · 28 mm shaft · bronze bushings or needle bearings · 1,600 lb rating (maker) · stiff whip · dual marks, no center knurl · black zinc · lifetime warranty",
    pros: [
      "The same bar with either bronze bushings or needle bearings, so you choose the spin",
